racts just under the limit, compared with 2% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 124 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,014 euros, was awarded in October 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical trends alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across different sectors to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the dates and amounts of contracts to identify patterns or repeated purchases. Contract [1] shows a single near-limit contract, which may be part of a broader trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["Dlsi2SB8TFCP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D","A%2FF8z0qYD6%2Fi0Kd8%2Brcp6w%3D%3D","0dwVXg%2FJB2p9Zh%2FyRJgM8w%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}